      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are pointing out the inherent tension between urgency and equity in policy design. Critics argue that framing the transition solely as an \"absolute\" deadline risks treating social concerns merely as implementation hurdles rather than co-equal priorities. From this skeptical viewpoint, the economic resistance signals a fundamental disagreement about whether climate risk is an *existential* emergency demanding immediate sacrifice, or a *manageable* externality that dictates a slower, more phased approach. The debate often centers on whether the urgency of the climate crisis permits—or demands—the sidelining of certain immediate economic considerations.",
      "source": "target",
